Let cache and preload follow the literal loader invocation directory.

Payload invocation selects the payload etc directory; /lib64 invocation
selects /etc in the current root, even when lib64 is a symlink.
Remove the final directory component lexically before opening the file;
passing /lib64/../etc to the kernel follows the symlink before its .. and
would incorrectly read /usr/etc when /lib64 points to /usr/lib64.
Unknown or relative interpreter names preserve the configured fallback.
No environment variable selects the cache, and the existing secure-mode
preload environment rule is retained.

